Figure  7  shows the distribution of the MAPE of 25x and 1000x magnification for each fold with increasing error. Using  YS  as example property with moderate performance the MAPE is at 5.8% (25x) and 8.2% (1000x), respectively. In the literature, typically 10%-30% of data points are used for final evaluation, which in this case equals up to 14 specimens. If 14 specimens would be chosen only once and randomly as validation data, the MAPE now ranges between 0.5%−26.5% for 25x and 0.7%−33.5% for 1000x magnification (the dashed lines in the figure indicate the 14 folds with lowest/highest error). A significant difference, that may even increase when fewer samples are selected, resulting in a biased model evaluation. Consequently, when only limited data is available, all samples should be used for testing in a cross-validation approach.
