This study demonstrates the critical importance of robust dataset splitting strategies in machine learning workflows involving microstructural image data. Specifically, the artificially inflated performance by invalid splitting as observed in the comparison of different split strategies (RQ2) highlights the importance of independent training and validation data. Micrographs of the same specimen must always be contained within the same data split. For instance on our data, the mean absolute percentage error (MAPE) and normalized MAE decrease by up to a factor of three, and  R 2 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
